#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:108
#: e05f1d4cbec54dae8d9fe4e73a4f6339
msgid "How it works"
msgstr "工作原理"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:110
#: 4e130fa69ba343d29012326f11a8653d
msgid ""
"The mouse sensor returns the average movement (in the x and y directions) of"
" surface features that it sees. A single pixel move will not cause the "
"sensor to return \"1\". It will return a higher value around 5. This value "
"is referred to as the **scaler** below. In the example below, the value "
"returned would be about 1.6 ( (-5+5+5) / 3)"
msgstr ""
"鼠标传感器返回其所看到的表面特征在 x 和 y 方向上的平均移动量。单个像素的移动不会使传感器返回「1」，而会返回约 5 "
"的较高值，即下文所称的**缩放系数**。在下面的示例中，返回值约为 1.6（(-5+5+5) / 3）"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:119
#: d66524cdd8b6456ebe47d1a1d8c7d353
msgid ""
"**Sensor's x and y values can be converted to real distances based on "
"altitude**"
msgstr "**传感器的 x 和 y 值可根据高度换算为实际距离**"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:122
#: f9ead9164b0c4ba2ad4f378625fdf4e6
msgid ""
"In order to convert values from the sensor to real distances moved, we need "
"to take into account the altitude. This is necessary because as you can see "
"from the two pictures below, if we have two quads moving the same distance, "
"but one at a low altitude, the other at a higher altitude, the lower quad "
"will see surface features appear to move further and this will result in a "
"higher optical flow values"
msgstr ""
"为了将传感器的数值转换为实际移动距离，需要考虑高度因素。这是必要的，因为如下图所示，如果两架四轴飞行器移动相同距离，但一架在低空、另一架在高空，低空的那架看到的表面特征移动幅度更大，导致光流值更高"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:135
#: 0924603317cf4a51b898f58065d50c15
msgid "We compensate for vehicle roll and pitch changes"
msgstr "我们补偿飞行器横滚和俯仰变化"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:137
#: 210418b492cd4773972000c1954fcf15
msgid ""
"Change in the vehicle's roll and pitch will also cause changes in the x and "
"y values returned by the sensor. Unlike the lateral movement calculations "
"these are not dependent upon the distance of the visible objects. In the "
"picture below you can see that as the quad has rolled 10 degrees but both "
"flowers have moved from the center of the camera's view in the 1st pic to "
"the edge of the view in the 2nd pic."
msgstr ""
"飞行器横滚和俯仰的变化也会导致传感器返回的 x 和 y 值发生变化。与横向移动计算不同，这些变化不依赖于可见物体的距离。如下图所示，四轴飞行器横滚了 "
"10 度，两朵花都从第 1 张图中相机视野的中心移动到了第 2 张图中视野的边缘。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:147
#: 0ec17f750bff4cdc982f7fbb44c3bb62
msgid ""
"The expected change in sensor values can be calculated directly from the "
"change in roll and pitch given the formula below. We subtract these expected"
" changes from the real values returned by the sensor."
msgstr "根据下方公式，可以直接从横滚和俯仰的变化量计算出传感器值的预期变化量，然后从传感器实际返回的值中减去这些预期变化量。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:154
#: fe97cabcd4d34fcfa304b8e2594c04bf
msgid ""
"Once we have the x/y movements we can integrate these values over time with "
"the current yaw to arrive at an estimate of position."
msgstr "得到 x/y 方向的移动量后，我们可以结合当前偏航将这些值随时间积分，从而得出位置估计。"

